This VERSION file is the authoritative build identifier.
All visible labels, launcher, and window titles must match this version.

v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application, replacing a five-file
browser prototype that was reviewed and found not releasable.

v2.1.0 added a Tie bet alongside Banker or Player, moved the disclaimer to the foot of the window and
removed page scrolling. v2.2.x put the panels beside the betting column for half-screen use, gave the
bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box of small colour-only hands and renamed the panels. v2.3.0 made PASS
record the table's result. v2.4.0 gave the Tie insurance its own stake.

v2.5.0 added the OCR spot-check tool, an accuracy readout and a working Gemini model id. v2.5.1 proved
the reading prompt against synthetic displays and made that check gradable. v2.5.2 added a
"Save a screenshot sample" button. v2.6.0 is where the reader met the real table: all four real
screenshots read correctly, and three defects surfaced that synthetic images had hidden (truncated
replies discarded, a reasoning model returning nothing on a cluttered image, empty replies not
retried). It also removed a private file that had been synced to the public repository, and the sync
now refuses images outright. v2.7.0 adds one-click calibration: the module finds the user's saved
table screenshot on the live screen, reports the match score and writes the region into the profile —
refusing rather than guessing when the match is poor.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
